        "entwurfsbeschreibung": "UMAR is a research apartment designed as a catalogue of reversible material cycles. Most components are selected for separability, take-back, reuse, recycling or compostability; reclaimed Jules Wabbes door handles add a small but explicit reused-component layer. The architectural output is a clean demonstrator rather than a salvage collage: dry joints, modular layers, visible systems and controlled material contrasts show how a dwelling can be designed for future disassembly and resource recovery.",
